        "question_text": "<p>According to Boyle's Law, what happens to the volume of a gas if its pressure is doubled at constant temperature?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Boyle's Law states that the pressure of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature ($P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}$). If pressure is doubled, the volume is halved.</p>",
